1
00:00:00,610 --> 00:00:02,950
The class bike ride starts in one hour!

2
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:04,642
Ta-da!

3
00:00:05,152 --> 00:00:06,732
My Super-Light Racer!

4
00:00:07,212 --> 00:00:09,633
I took off every part that does nothing.

5
00:00:10,062 --> 00:00:11,912
Lighter bike, faster bike!

6
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:13,983
Ready, steady...

7
00:00:14,194 --> 00:00:15,323
whoa, whoa, whoa!

8
00:00:17,996 --> 00:00:19,736
Lightest bike in Singapore.

9
00:00:20,076 --> 00:00:21,396
Also the slowest.

10
00:00:22,042 --> 00:00:22,682
Pip!

11
00:00:23,102 --> 00:00:25,032
Which parts did you take off?

12
00:00:25,678 --> 00:00:27,348
Only the boring ones.

13
00:00:27,768 --> 00:00:29,688
Don't worry, I've got a plan!

14
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:31,740
That's how this started.

15
00:00:32,649 --> 00:00:34,279
The Great Bike Breakdown!

16
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:37,217
Plan one: I pedal harder.

17
00:00:37,727 --> 00:00:39,177
Much, much harder!

18
00:00:40,205 --> 00:00:43,405
Plan two: we loop Momo's skipping rope round the gears.

19
00:00:44,426 --> 00:00:47,016
Plan three: put back the chain you took off.

20
00:00:48,038 --> 00:00:49,078
The chain?

21
00:00:49,578 --> 00:00:53,258
It just goes round and round, and it makes my socks black!

22
00:00:53,904 --> 00:00:55,764
Which fix gets the bike moving?

23
00:00:56,044 --> 00:00:58,174
Show me one, two or three fingers!

24
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:05,930
One!

25
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:08,160
My legs are super strong!

26
00:01:09,113 --> 00:01:09,773
Two.

27
00:01:10,123 --> 00:01:11,353
A loop is a loop.

28
00:01:12,301 --> 00:01:12,881
Three.

29
00:01:13,471 --> 00:01:16,061
If it was on the bike, maybe it had a job.

30
00:01:17,013 --> 00:01:18,163
Three fixes.

31
00:01:18,443 --> 00:01:19,613
Let's test them!

32
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:21,742
Fix one.

33
00:01:22,012 --> 00:01:23,412
Pip pedals harder!

34
00:01:24,058 --> 00:01:25,978
Faster, faster, FASTER!

35
00:01:28,693 --> 00:01:31,623
The pedals spin, but the back wheel isn't moving!

36
00:01:31,895 --> 00:01:34,398
Let's look at that again, in slow motion.

37
00:01:34,418 --> 00:01:38,676
Faster, faster, FASTER!

38
00:01:39,447 --> 00:01:43,087
The front gear turns, but nothing joins it to the back wheel.

39
00:01:43,347 --> 00:01:46,957
Pushing harder on one part cannot do another part's job.

40
00:01:48,286 --> 00:01:49,346
Strong legs.

41
00:01:49,626 --> 00:01:50,736
Going nowhere.

42
00:01:51,682 --> 00:01:52,732
Fix two.

43
00:01:52,992 --> 00:01:55,332
The skipping rope goes round both gears.

44
00:01:56,282 --> 00:01:59,352
Lift the back wheel, turn the pedal, and watch the magic.

45
00:02:02,861 --> 00:02:04,991
The magic is on your head, Basil.

46
00:02:05,944 --> 00:02:07,094
Look closer.

47
00:02:07,684 --> 00:02:10,754
Here is the chain from Pip's box of useless parts.

48
00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:13,370
See the gaps in the chain?

49
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:16,430
Each tooth of the gear fits into one, so when the gear

50
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:18,660
turns, it pulls the chain along.

51
00:02:19,913 --> 00:02:23,333
The chain pulls the back gear, and the back wheel turns.

52
00:02:23,913 --> 00:02:26,873
A smooth rope has no gaps, so the teeth slip.

53
00:02:28,212 --> 00:02:29,932
So the chain has a function.

54
00:02:30,272 --> 00:02:32,532
A function is a part's special job.

55
00:02:32,852 --> 00:02:36,112
The chain's job is to turn the back wheel when you pedal.

56
00:02:37,177 --> 00:02:38,897
So my rope had no function.

57
00:02:39,237 --> 00:02:40,097
Noted.

58
00:02:40,446 --> 00:02:42,556
Be one little link of the bike chain!

59
00:02:42,836 --> 00:02:43,826
Shrink down.

60
00:02:44,106 --> 00:02:45,036
Quietly.

61
00:02:46,892 --> 00:02:49,482
You are a link at the top of the chain, between the

62
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:50,532
two gears.

63
00:02:52,115 --> 00:02:53,875
Someone pushes the pedals.

64
00:02:54,635 --> 00:02:57,555
The front gear's teeth grab you and pull you forward.

65
00:02:58,144 --> 00:03:01,764
The whole chain moves with you, and tugs the back gear round.

66
00:03:02,544 --> 00:03:04,054
The back wheel turns!

67
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:08,590
Round the front gear you go, back underneath, and round again.

68
00:03:10,446 --> 00:03:11,476
Fix three.

69
00:03:11,746 --> 00:03:13,306
The chain goes back on.

70
00:03:13,971 --> 00:03:16,131
Lift the back wheel, and turn the pedal...

71
00:03:18,447 --> 00:03:19,087
It spins!

72
00:03:19,107 --> 00:03:21,667
The back wheel spins!

73
00:03:22,541 --> 00:03:24,301
Pedals, gear, chain, wheel.

74
00:03:24,741 --> 00:03:26,641
Each part acts on the next one.

75
00:03:27,668 --> 00:03:31,188
Scientists say the parts interact: they act on one another.

76
00:03:32,104 --> 00:03:34,354
Even I can't argue with a spinning wheel.

77
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,480
Pip, before you ride, squeeze the brakes.

78
00:03:38,132 --> 00:03:38,922
Squeeze...

79
00:03:39,582 --> 00:03:43,962
squeeze... Oh. I took those off too.

80
00:03:44,611 --> 00:03:45,251
Pip!

81
00:03:45,691 --> 00:03:48,201
A bike that cannot stop is not safe!

82
00:03:48,853 --> 00:03:52,553
The brakes help the bike stop safely, and the bell warns people.

83
00:03:52,863 --> 00:03:54,903
Every part has its own function.

84
00:03:58,198 --> 00:03:59,298
Quick question!

85
00:03:59,578 --> 00:04:02,168
If the bell falls off on the ride, can the bike still

86
00:04:02,188 --> 00:04:02,878
move?

87
00:04:03,158 --> 00:04:04,308
Think about it.

88
00:04:08,119 --> 00:04:10,509
It can still move, but it is not as safe!

89
00:04:11,388 --> 00:04:12,158
Yes!

90
00:04:12,428 --> 00:04:16,008
When one part stops working, the whole system is likely to be

91
00:04:16,028 --> 00:04:16,848
affected.

92
00:04:18,183 --> 00:04:19,653
So the bike is a system.

93
00:04:20,003 --> 00:04:23,143
A system is made up of different parts, and each part has

94
00:04:23,163 --> 00:04:24,943
its own special function.

95
00:04:26,497 --> 00:04:29,107
With one minute to spare, Pip makes the ride!

96
00:04:30,204 --> 00:04:31,404
Pip, you're puffing!

97
00:04:31,734 --> 00:04:33,954
Is something inside you broken too?

98
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:35,720
Nothing is broken.

99
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:37,450
Look closer.

100
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:40,630
Pip's bones and muscles move his legs.

101
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:44,340
His heart beats faster, and he breathes faster.

102
00:04:48,289 --> 00:04:50,469
So Pip's body is made of systems too.

103
00:04:50,839 --> 00:04:52,159
Very furry ones.

104
00:04:52,514 --> 00:04:54,954
And the ride ends under a giant rain tree.

105
00:04:56,069 --> 00:04:57,629
And a tree is a system too.

106
00:04:57,949 --> 00:05:01,549
Its leaves, its stem and its roots each have their own function.

107
00:05:02,879 --> 00:05:05,279
Now, here are the words that earn marks.

108
00:05:05,336 --> 00:05:06,486
Say it with me!

109
00:05:07,201 --> 00:05:09,421
A system is made up of different parts.

110
00:05:09,701 --> 00:05:11,431
Each part has its own function.

111
00:05:11,721 --> 00:05:13,901
The parts interact to perform a function.

112
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:17,611
When one part stops working, the whole system is likely to be

113
00:05:17,631 --> 00:05:18,561
affected.

114
00:05:21,034 --> 00:05:23,854
Basil, your tail doesn't pedal, and it doesn't ring.

115
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:26,294
Lighter lizard, faster lizard?

116
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:28,550
My tail helps me balance.

117
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:30,690
Every part has a function, Pip.

118
00:05:31,339 --> 00:05:32,459
Ring, ring!

119
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:34,319
My bell works!

120
00:05:35,346 --> 00:05:36,436
Picked the chain?

121
00:05:36,716 --> 00:05:38,756
You win a point, and so does Momo!

122
00:05:41,444 --> 00:05:42,704
Excuse me.

123
00:05:43,234 --> 00:05:45,544
I'm watered every single day.

124
00:05:46,044 --> 00:05:48,124
So why am I wilting?

125
00:05:48,775 --> 00:05:51,085
Next time, at the Plant Help Desk!

126
00:05:51,808 --> 00:05:54,008
Let's read today's key words together!

127
00:05:54,298 --> 00:05:55,058
Ready?

128
00:05:55,345 --> 00:05:56,185
System.

129
00:05:57,555 --> 00:05:58,435
Function.

130
00:05:59,739 --> 00:06:00,589
Interact.

131
00:06:02,128 --> 00:06:03,068
Well done!

132
00:06:04,050 --> 00:06:05,151
Say it with us!

133
00:06:05,951 --> 00:06:06,701
Ready?

134
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:07,484
One!

135
00:06:07,824 --> 00:06:08,524
two!

136
00:06:08,829 --> 00:06:10,004
Now you know!

137
00:06:15,014 --> 00:06:16,874
Lighter bike, faster bike!

138
00:06:16,924 --> 00:06:17,967
Lighter bike.

139
00:06:17,987 --> 00:06:19,277
Not faster.
